        "original_id": "32930fe3-4693-59d4-ad1d-bd91dc2c4c7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Countries: Russia, United Kingdom\n- Events: World War I, World War II, Cold War, Russian Revolution, February Revolution\n- People: Emperor Nicholas II\n- Governments: Russian Empire, provisional government\n\nFacts:\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies during World War I, but their relations were strained by the Russian Revolution of 1917.\n- In the first revolution of February 1917, dated March 1917 in the Gregorian calendar, Emperor Nicholas II abdicated and the Russian Empire collapsed.\n- After the collapse of the old regime in 1917, a provisional government replaced it in Russia.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies again during World War II.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were hostile rivals during the Cold War from 1947 to 1991.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "26a704df-d6bc-511a-876b-f32e34a77816",
        "text": "Page: Russia–United Kingdom relations. Sentence: They were allies again in World Wars I and II, although relations were strained by the Russian Revolution of 1917.\nPage: Russia–United Kingdom relations. Sentence: They were at sword's point during the Cold War (1947–91).\nPage: Russian Revolution. Sentence: The Russian Empire collapsed with the abdication of Emperor Nicholas II and the old regime was replaced by a provisional government during the first revolution of February 1917 (March in the Gregorian calendar; the older Julian calendar was in use in Russia at the time).",
